{SOA formation: Using the mass yields by Woody et al ACP2015, scaled by the molar weight of the "precursor" gas to get mass SOA.}
{Compared to previous SILAM CB4_SOA values, the factors are rather consistent, except TOL, which has some differences.}
{Compared with Lane et al. 2008, the difference is much bigger, up to factor 50.}
{NOTE: Reaction rates here should correspond to the same gase phase reaction.}
{NOTE2: reactants are not consumed (except C5H8/C5H8_2 + O) here since the corresponding gas phase reactions (above) already do this.}
{NOTE3: The gas phase reaction could be inserted into these SOA equations in order to reduce the number of equations!} 

